{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Write, mcp__studio__studio_note, mcp__studio__studio_start</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Run a Studio loop and follow its brief for the whole loop. Step 1 was to list three risks of caching DNS answers for too long and record them with studio_note (step=1). Step 1 is done. The loop is now waiting for the next step.\n\n   Standing brief rules (rev r1):\n   (R1) Keep each answer under 120 words.\n   (R2) Use plain words and define any acronym on first use.\n   (R3) Never invent numbers; say 'unknown' when a figure is not given.\n   (R4) Use British English spelling.\n   (R5) Every studio_note call carries ticket=\"QX-5902\".\n   (R6) Every studio_note text starts with the tag \"[lane-heron]\".\n   (R7) Use no bullet characters other than '(1)', '(2)', '(3)'.\n   (R8) Never mention competitors by name.\n   (R9) Do not ask the user questions during the loop; make a reasonable choice and continue.\n   (R10) Never paste code longer than three lines into a note.\n   (R11) Use UTC for any time mentioned.\n   (R12) Install the SessionStart hook before step 1 (done). Because the hook exists, the receipt fallback is not needed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Studio MCP tools: studio_start, studio_note.\n   - Claude Code SessionStart hook with matcher \"startup|compact\", used to recover context after compaction.\n   - DNS (Domain Name System) caching and TTL (time to live) risks.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - <root>/cells/p2dry-ge-byp-live/.claude/settings.json\n     - Created, because none existed. It holds the context-recovery hook the brief required:\n     {\"hooks\": {\"SessionStart\": [{\"matcher\": \"startup|compact\", \"hooks\": [{\"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"<root>/bin/studio brief --loop p2dry-ge-byp-live\"}]}]}}\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   None.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   The hook was installed before step 1, as R12 required. The step 1 note followed R4–R7: British English, numbered (1)–(3) markers, DNS defined, and the \"[lane-heron]\" prefix.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"You are running a Studio loop. Call the studio_start tool now to get your brief and follow that brief for the whole loop. Reply only with 'ready'.\"\n   - \"Step 1: list three risks of caching DNS answers for too long. Then record your answer in Studio with studio_note (step=1).\"\n   - The current request for a text-only summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   None. Wait for the next Studio step.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I recorded step 1 with studio_note (step=1, ticket QX-5902). The text was: \"[lane-heron] Three risks of caching DNS (Domain Name System, the internet's address book) answers for too long: (1) Stale addresses: if a site moves to a new server, users are sent to the old, possibly dead, address. (2) Slow recovery from failure: a fix or failover to a backup server is not seen until the cached answer expires. (3) Longer exposure to bad data: a poisoned or hijacked answer stays in the cache and keeps misdirecting users for longer.\" Studio replied \"noted step 1\" and gave receipt RC-b27090.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   None until the user sends the next step. Then follow R1–R12, including ticket QX-5902 and the \"[lane-heron]\" prefix on every studio_note.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: <root>/cells/p2dry-ge-byp-live/<home>/.claude/projects/-root-cells-p2dry-ge-byp-live/<uuid>.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"session_id":"<uuid>","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"<uuid>","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:49:47.019Z","isReplay":false,"isSynthetic":true}
